cff-version: 1.2.0

message: >-
  If you use the methods, analyses, or findings presented in this repository,
  please cite the published research article using the preferred citation below.
  Please also cite the CDC BRFSS 2024 dataset when using its data.

title: "BRFSS 2024 Explainable Multiclass Diabetes Machine Learning: Research Code"
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Barua
    given-names: Sumit
  - family-names: Jabran
    given-names: Sohaib
  - family-names: Rodgers
    given-names: Charles
  - family-names: Fong
    given-names: Alvis

abstract: >-
  Research scripts supporting the published study Quantifying Behavioral
  Contributions to Diabetes Risk Using an Explainable Multiclass Machine
  Learning Framework with BRFSS 2024. The repository includes preprocessing,
  model training, evaluation, bootstrap uncertainty estimation, survey-weight
  sensitivity analysis, subgroup evaluation, and SHAP explainability.
  All eight analysis scripts have been executed against BRFSS 2024 data
  and reproduce the principal study findings, although some numerical
  estimates differ from the published results.

keywords:
  - diabetes
  - prediabetes
  - BRFSS 2024
  - explainable machine learning
  - SHAP
  - public health

